index 0000000..e4e3464
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+# The Daily Grind
+
+The homepage is a static site. Its Receipts & Gifts section uses native Web Crypto to create and verify signed JSON documents without sending document details to a server. Use HTTPS (or a browser-recognized secure local origin) with JavaScript and IndexedDB enabled.
+
+## Signing and verification
+
+- Choose a coffee receipt or gift voucher, enter details and a USD amount, and create a signed document. Download its JSON or send it to the verifier.
+- A non-exportable private key is generated once and saved in IndexedDB for this origin/browser profile. Clearing site data loses the signing key. The exported public key can still verify previously signed documents.
+- Native ML-DSA-65 is selected when the browser reports signing and verification support. Otherwise, signing falls back to Ed25519, then ECDSA P-256 with SHA-256. Verification uses the document's declared suite, never a downgraded algorithm.
+- The verifier trusts this browser's key by default. To verify another browser's documents, load the issuer's exported public key, compare its complete SHA-256 fingerprint through a trusted separate channel, and explicitly confirm trust. Imported trust lasts for the current page session. Embedded public keys are not accepted as proof of trust.
+- Version, suite, fingerprint, document type, issuer, ID, timestamp, description, amount, and currency are bound into a fixed, domain-separated signature input. JSON field order and formatting do not affect verification. Unknown fields and unsupported suites are rejected.
+
+## Trust boundary
+
+This repository has no merchant backend, authenticated merchant signer, checkout confirmation, or redemption ledger. Anyone opening the homepage can issue local documents. Signatures prove that signed content is unchanged and was signed by the corresponding trusted key; they do not prove a Daily Grind purchase, payment, merchant identity, or available voucher balance. The interface labels this explicitly.
+
+Production merchant issuance requires a protected merchant signing identity, public-key distribution through an authenticated channel, and an authoritative order/payment source. Redeemable vouchers also require expiry and redemption enforcement backed by a ledger. A merchant private key must never be bundled into this public site.
+
+## Checks
+
+`npm test` runs cryptographic tests using Node's Web Crypto implementation, without a browser or server. These cover round trips, tampering, signer substitution, key imports, malformed documents, and both classical fallback suites. Newer algorithms may produce Node experimental API warnings.
